Start screen: PLAY only, no subtitle, no star map. Top bar empty left. Hmm, the top bar looks like a big empty pill with stats at right. It might be visually odd. Should we remove the topbar background/border on start/home, making just floating stats? That would look cleaner and still satisfy "remove text". Let's consider. The topbar has right stats and sound. The empty left is ugly. Could restyle start/home topbar to be transparent/no border, right-aligned. But then it might blend. Maybe better. Since the user said "remove that text at the top called rebel command, because it's useless" - they may want the whole top header removed. But we kept the stats. Could remove the topbar entirely on start and home? That removes commander/best/units/sound. The sound could be settings via dock. For start, no settings button, but the sound toggle would be gone. Maybe okay, but losing best stats.

Alternative: rework start topbar to not be a full bar: use a compact right-aligned stat row without background. The empty bar is the only visual issue. Let's restyle for start/home:
```
.start-shell > .menu-topbar,
.hub-shell > .menu-topbar {
  justify-content: flex-end;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  background: none;
  box-shadow: none;
  backdrop-filter: none;
}
.start-shell > .menu-topbar::after,
.hub-shell > .menu-topbar::after { display: none; }
```
This leaves floating chips at top right, no empty bar. Better. But the topbar height still there, okay.

